## Explanation of Changes

1. **50-job enqueue limit**: The requirement shows one `enqueueJob` per case, but the nightly cleanup closes up to 200 cases in a single API transaction. Salesforce limits you to **50 Apex jobs enqueued per transaction**. A naive loop would throw a `LimitException` on the 51st call. I added a **chaining dispatcher**: when more than 50 cases qualify, the trigger enqueues a single `CaseSurveyJob` carrying the full ID list. That job dispatches 49 individual `CaseSurveyJob(caseId)` instances plus one more dispatcher for the remainder, keeping every transaction at ≤ 50 enqueues while still giving each case its own isolated job.

2. **Safety re-check in the job**: The job re-queries the Case and re-verifies `ContactId != null` before inserting the Task. This guards against a race condition where the contact is removed between the trigger firing and the job executing.

3. **`Trigger.oldMap` comparison**: The trigger uses `Trigger.oldMap.get(c.Id).IsClosed` to detect the `false → true` transition, so cases that were already closed (or toggled open) are correctly ignored.

---

File: force-app/main/default/triggers/CaseTrigger.trigger
```apex
trigger CaseTrigger on Case (after update) {

    List<Id> eligibleCaseIds = new List<Id>();

    for (Case c : Trigger.new) {
        Case oldC = Trigger.oldMap.get(c.Id);
        if (!oldC.IsClosed && c.IsClosed && c.ContactId != null) {
            eligibleCaseIds.add(c.Id);
        }
    }

    if (eligibleCaseIds.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }

    // Governor limit: max 50 Apex jobs enqueued per transaction.
    // When we stay within the limit, enqueue one job per case for full isolation.
    // When we exceed it, hand the full list to a single dispatcher job that
    // chains itself, still producing one independent job per case.
    if (eligibleCaseIds.size() <= 50) {
        for (Id cId : eligibleCaseIds) {
            System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(cId));
        }
    } else {
        System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(eligibleCaseIds));
    }
}
```

File: force-app/main/default/classes/CaseSurveyJob.cls
```apex
public class CaseSurveyJob implements Queueable {

    private static final Integer MAX_JOBS_PER_TX = 50;

    private Id    caseId;   // single-case mode
    private List<Id> caseIds; // dispatcher mode

    /**
     * Single-case constructor – used by the trigger (and by the dispatcher).
     */
    public CaseSurveyJob(Id caseId) {
        this.caseId = caseId;
    }

    /**
     * List constructor – used internally to chain when > 50 cases are eligible.
     */
    public CaseSurveyJob(List<Id> caseIds) {
        this.caseIds = caseIds;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext ctx) {
        if (caseId != null) {
            processSingleCase(caseId);
        } else if (caseIds != null && !caseIds.isEmpty()) {
            dispatch(caseIds);
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Dispatcher: enqueues up to (MAX_JOBS_PER_TX - 1) individual jobs plus
    // one more dispatcher for the remainder, keeping every transaction ≤ 50.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void dispatch(List<Id> ids) {
        if (ids.size() <= MAX_JOBS_PER_TX) {
            // Everything fits in one transaction – enqueue individually.
            for (Id id : ids) {
                System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(id));
            }
            return;
        }

        // Reserve one slot for the next dispatcher.
        Integer chunkSize = MAX_JOBS_PER_TX - 1; // 49
        List<Id> firstChunk  = ids.sublist(0, chunkSize);
        List<Id> remaining   = ids.sublist(chunkSize, ids.size());

        for (Id id : firstChunk) {
            System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(id));
        }

        // 49 individual + 1 dispatcher = 50 total (within the limit).
        System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(remaining));
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Core work: create the CSAT survey Task for one Case.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void processSingleCase(Id cId) {
        Case theCase = [
            SELECT Id, CaseNumber, ContactId
            FROM Case
            WHERE Id = :cId
        ];

        // Re-check: the contact may have been removed after the trigger fired.
        if (theCase.ContactId == null) {
            return;
        }

        Task t = new Task(
            WhatId      = theCase.Id,
            WhoId       = theCase.ContactId,
            Subject     = 'CSAT survey: ' + theCase.CaseNumber,
            ActivityDate = Date.today().addDays(2),
            Status      = 'Not Started'
        );

        insert t;
    }
}
```

